            <ArticleTitle>A teenager with an annoying cough.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>349-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic cough is a stressful condition and can lead to extensive investigations. Bronchial asthma and postnasal drip syndrome are common causes, but sometimes the origin of cough is outside the respiratory tract (1,2). Such a relatively simple test as esophageal pH probing may suggest appropriate (antireflux) therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
